        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/VT_0002100"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Any measurable or observable characteristic related to the shape, structure, color or pattern of the fibrous connective tissue that surrounds the root of a tooth, separating it from and attaching it to the alveolar bone; normally extends from the base of the gingival mucosa to the fundus of the bony socket, and its main function is to hold the tooth in its socket.</obo:IAO_0000115>
