        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/VT_0000031"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Any measurable or observable characteristic related to the shape, structure, color or pattern of the Reissner&apos;s membrane which separates the cochlear duct from the vestibular canal, i.e., the endolymph of the scala media from the perilymph of the scala vestibuli; the Reissner membrane consists of squamous epithelial cells with microvilli toward the ductus, a basement membrane, and a thin layer of connective tissue toward the scala.</obo:IAO_0000115>
